      "description": "Watch Falkirk vs Rangers highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 2, 2026. The Scottish Premiership season continued with intensity on September 2nd, 2026 , as Falkirk hosted Rangers in a match filled with tactical battles and individual brilliance. Both sides took to the pitch under the floodlights, eager to claim dominance in this high-stakes encounter. Early Breakthrough Sets the Tone The atmosphere was electric as the match kicked off, and it didn't take long for the visitors to make their mark. In the 8th minute, Djeidi Gassama delivered a precise pass to Lawrence Shankland , who clinically finished to put Rangers ahead. The early goal forced Falkirk to adjust their game plan, but the visitors continued to press with high energy. Disaster struck for the home side just before the interval. In the 44th minute, Kosta Nedeljkovic accidentally turned the ball into his own net, doubling the lead for the opposition. It was a cruel blow for Falkirk , who had been fighting to stay in the contest despite the early setback, leaving them with a mountain to climb in the second half. Tactical Shifts and Late Drama The second half saw a rise in tension, with the referee busy as Ethan Ross , Brad Spencer , and Olwethu Makhanya all received yellow cards in quick succession. As both managers turned to their benches, Ross McCrorie replaced Nedeljkovic and immediately made an impact on the flank. In the 79th minute, the victory was secured when Ross McCrorie provided a perfectly timed assist for Lawrence Shankland , who netted his second goal of the night. With the result beyond doubt, Rangers managed the closing stages professionally, bringing on Ben Godfrey to see out the final minutes and ensure a clean sheet and a vital three points on the road."
