      "description": "Watch Falkirk vs ST Mirren highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 1, 2026. The stage was set on August 1, 2026 , as Falkirk played host to St. Mirren in a highly anticipated Premiership encounter. Both sets of fans filled the stands, eager to see their teams compete in a match that promised plenty of tactical intrigue and competitive spirit. Early Breakthrough for the Visitors St. Mirren started the match with clear intent, applying pressure from the opening whistle. Their persistence paid off in the 11th minute when Henry Fieldson delivered a pinpoint assist to find Killian Phillips . The forward made no mistake, clinical in his execution to give his side an early lead. Falkirk attempted to find an immediate response, but the visitors' defensive line held firm, ensuring they went into the break with their advantage intact despite the growing pressure from the home side. Tactical Shifts and Rising Tension As the second half progressed, the match became a more cagey affair with both managers turning to their benches. St. Mirren introduced Roland Idowu in the 83rd minute, looking to secure the result, while Falkirk made several changes, including bringing on Paul McGovern and Leon McCann . The referee was kept busy as the physical nature of the game increased, issuing yellow cards to Ryan Carr and Henry Fieldson as both teams battled fiercely for control of the midfield. Phillips Doubles the Advantage The defining moment arrived late in the game. In the 87th minute, Roland Idowu made an immediate impact, providing the assist for Killian Phillips to strike again. His second goal of the match effectively ended Falkirk's hopes of a comeback. Although Phillips and Luke Thomas both picked up late bookings in a heated conclusion, St. Mirren navigated the final minutes and five minutes of stoppage time to claim a deserved victory on the road."
